      "id": "summary",
      "proposition": {
        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>Readers respond to a report on the tragic consequences of the ‘care cliff’, when vital support is taken away at age 18</p><p>Your article draws attention to a landmark review that describes the “care cliff” for young people leaving care at 18 leading to tragic outcomes (<a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/aug/25/he-was-left-on-his-own-the-care-leaver-lives-lost-to-a-system-that-abandons-them-at-18\">‘He was left on his own’: the care-leaver lives lost to a system that abandons them at 18, 25 August</a>). The good news is that there are ways to fix this problem, but they are neither quick nor straightforward.</p><p>My own <a href=\"https://www.academia.edu/5168676/Kinship_Care_Research_Evidence_publication_for_the_governments_Centre_for_Social_Justice_CSJ_\">research</a> found that first and foremost the responsible local authority requires sufficient funding, staffing and planning to assess and implement care options when a child is taken into care.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/sep/01/we-must-do-more-to-save-care-leavers-lives\">Continue reading...</a>"
      },
